<div class="calcpad-output">
 <!-- Plane-stress analysis of a simply-supported deep beam under a partial uniform load, using a sine-series decomposition of the load and reaction.
<p>Recovers $σ_x$, $σ_y$ and $τ_{xy}$ for arbitrary length, height, load span and support width — an analytical baseline for FE checks. -->
 <h3>Input data</h3>
 <table>
  <tr>
   <td>
    <p>
     Beam length -
     <span class="eq">
      <var>l</var>
      =
      <u class="input-6">4</u>
      <i>m</i>
     </span>
    </p>
    <p>
     Height -
     <span class="eq">
      <var>h</var>
      =
      <u class="input-7">2</u>
      <i>m</i>
     </span>
    </p>
    <p>
     Load -
     <span class="eq">
      <var>q</var>
      =
      <u class="input-8">100</u>
      <span class="dvc">
       <i>kN</i>
       <span class="dvl">
       </span>
       <i>m</i>
      </span>
     </span>
    </p>
    <p>
     Length of load -
     <span class="eq">
      <var>b</var>
      =
      <u class="input-9">0.8</u>
      <i>m</i>
     </span>
    </p>
    <p>
     Distance to load start -
     <span class="eq">
      <var>a</var>
      =
      <u class="input-10">1.6</u>
      <i>m</i>
     </span>
    </p>
    <p>
     Length of support -
     <span class="eq">
      <var>d</var>
      =
      <u class="input-11">0.4</u>
      <i>m</i>
     </span>
    </p>
    <p>
     Number of iterations -
     <span class="eq">
      <var>N</var>
      =
      <u class="input-12">21</u>
     </span>
    </p>
   </td>
   <td>
    <img src="Images/mechanics/elastic/deep-beam-fea.png" style="height:160pt; width:150pt; margin-left:50pt;"/>
   </td>
  </tr>
 </table>
 <p>Original and Fourier functions for the load</p>
